# The estate serves LF. Netlify stores what we upload, byte for byte, and
# release_check.py compares local bytes against the live sha, so a CRLF file
# is a content difference on five revenue subdomains, not a cosmetic one.
#
# Without this file and with core.autocrlf=true (the default on this box), a
# fresh clone checked out 375 CRLF files against 7 LF, and building from that
# clone produced a deploy artefact differing from the validated one in 109 of
# 136 files -- 59,196 bytes of pure line-ending churn. The build was therefore
# reproducible only inside one working directory. Found by audit 2026-09-09.
#
# eol=lf pins the WORKING TREE, not just the stored blob, so it holds no
# matter what core.autocrlf is set to on the machine doing the clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these, and never diff them as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.avif binary
*.pdf  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
